        "output_semantics": "Each prediction slot is [dx,dy,dz,r1x,r1y,r1z,r2x,r2y,r2z,g]. Position is in world metres relative to a fresh-observation continuous relational anchor: a normalized blend of current container, bowl and marked-return origins. The blend is determined only from current container elevation/uprightness and observed particle geometry. The six rotation values are the first two columns of the desired TCP rotation in the current observed container frame and are projected by Gram-Schmidt; g preserves the demonstrated native gripper scalar. Slots represent t-1 through t+14 and execution uses slots 1 through 8. For every executed slot, the fresh current observation reconstructs a world TCP pose; panda_kinematics.solve_ik converts it from freshly measured qpos to seven absolute Panda joint targets. The relational anchor is a coordinate conversion, not a scripted action or stage controller.",
